 /*
- * The backlight CoreBrightness drives (BrightnessControl's BCAppleBacklightBrtControl): a
- * service of its own that says backlight-control, gives its range in nits and is told a
- * brightness through setProperties. backlight-control on AppleCLCD itself made QuartzCore take
- * the framebuffer for one with frame-synchronous brightness and backboardd stopped drawing
- * (all8). Opt-in (sweetbacklight=2) until a boot shows what QuartzCore does with this one;
- * every property set on it is logged, and a nits value goes to the panel.
+ * Panel brightness for CoreBrightness (backboardd), as ios-sailfish 0168 does it: CoreBrightness
+ * takes the service with backlight-control = true that conforms to AppleARMBacklight, reads min
+ * and max from IODisplayParameters and sets {brightness = ceil(level * (max - min)) + min,
+ * FadePeriod = seconds as 16.16, backlight-level} with IORegistryEntrySetCFProperties. 0..255 is
+ * mapped onto the panel's DCS 0x51 range (1..0x7ff); the fade is stepped here every 16 ms on its
+ * own work loop. Our first tries (backlight-control on AppleCLCD, then a service of our own class
+ * with nits keys) stalled backboardd (all8, all13bl, all14bl): the wrong class and no
+ * IODisplayParameters. Opt-in with sweetbacklight=2.
  */
